<!--
  RSW_TaozinGrub — TAOZIN SPLIT, 2026-10-17. Owner, facings sheet (verbatim in
  design/RimStarWars/taozin_split_proposal_2026-10-17.md): "The second creature is the Taozin Grub, a much
  smaller creature as large as an arm that is a major component of Star Wars Cuisine mod and can be found only in
  Taozin nests." Canon brief: design/RimStarWars/canon_references/taozin_grub/description.md.

  - Never wild on the open map: no wildBiomes, no roster row. Its only entry is the nest set piece
    (MapGeneration/RSW_TaozinNest.xml) on Crags (RM_Abyss) maps, beside a guarding adult RSW_Taozin.
  - Tameable (Wildness 0.6), harmless, slow; it barely leaves the nest.
  - Colour (owner ruling, canon_references/taozin_grub ## ruling): terracotta by default; WHITE after long brine.
    Today only the terracotta look is wired (texPath below). The white look and the brine-tank production that
    triggers it need C# and are the filed follow-up TAOZIN_BRINE_TANK_BUILD_GRUB_GOES_PALE (art for both looks is queued).
  - Grub brine (RSW_TaozinBrine) lives in the Cuisine mod (mandrake.rsw.cuisine).
  PROVISIONAL numbers: every stat below is INVENTED for a forearm-length grub, pending the owner's review.
-->
<Defs>
  <ThingDef ParentName="AnimalThingBase">
    <defName>RSW_TaozinGrub</defName>
    <label>taozin grub</label>
    <description>The grub of the giant taozin: a terracotta, forearm-long creature with eight pairs of short dark legs bunched behind its blunt head, a pale banded collar and a long whip of a tail. Kept in brine it lies sedated and slowly infuses the liquid with a delicacy said to steady the mind, and a grub kept so long enough fades to white. Grubs are found only in taozin nests, under the guard of an adult.</description>
